! The band structure of the ten-site silicon supercell, on the density
! `si10-nc.in` converges (the `-bands` suffix is the naming convention the
! reference generator reads that dependency from).
!
! The path is in **crystal** coordinates of the supercell. Its first leg,
! `(0,0,1/2) -> (0,0,0)`, runs along the direction the five primitive cells were
! stacked in, so the primitive band structure comes back **folded five times**
! along it -- twenty bands where the primitive cell has four. That folding is
! the check with real content here: a supercell's bands are the primitive ones
! sampled at five shifted wavevectors, and nothing in either code imposes it.
! The remaining legs cross the two short reciprocal vectors.
!
! `nbnd = 26` puts six empty bands above the twenty occupied ones, so the
! comparison reaches the conduction band where the two codes' agreement is
! worst.
 &control
    calculation = 'bands'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 0, celldm(1) = 10.20, nat = 10, ntyp = 1,
    ecutwfc = 12.0
    nbnd = 26
 /
 &electrons
 /
CELL_PARAMETERS alat
  -0.50  0.00  0.50
   0.00  0.50  0.50
  -2.50  2.50  0.00
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Si  28.086  Si.pz-vbc.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (alat)
 Si    0.0000    0.0000    0.0000
 Si    0.2500    0.2500    0.2500
 Si   -0.5000    0.5000    0.0000
 Si   -0.2500    0.7500    0.2500
 Si   -1.0000    1.0000    0.0000
 Si   -0.7500    1.2500    0.2500
 Si   -1.5000    1.5000    0.0000
 Si   -1.2500    1.7500    0.2500
 Si   -2.0000    2.0000    0.0000
 Si   -1.7500    2.2500    0.2500
K_POINTS crystal_b
  4
  0.00  0.00  0.50 6
  0.00  0.00  0.00 6
  0.50  0.00  0.00 6
  0.50  0.50  0.00 1
